No campaign may be launched with unapproved spending or unsupported product claims.

13. FUTURE PAYMENTS AND FINANCIAL CONTROLS

Live payments are outside the initial static website release. They require a separate approval and implementation process.

13.1 Payment requirements

Before activation:

- Confirm the authorized merchant and settlement account.
- Verify the provider's current fees, eligibility, settlement rules and supported methods.
- Test in the provider's sandbox or equivalent test environment.
- Protect credentials server-side.
- Validate payment notifications using the provider's documented security mechanism.
- Handle pending, successful, failed, cancelled, refunded, reversed and disputed payments.
- Prevent duplicate orders and duplicate financial entries.
- Reconcile orders against trusted provider records.
- Never store raw card numbers or card security codes.
- Never treat a customer screenshot as sufficient proof of payment.

13.2 Commission calculation

The store's gross receipts must not be routed through the agency's personal account.

The commission system must follow a written agreement defining:

- Commission rate or calculation method.
- Eligible products or sales.
- When commission is earned.
- Treatment of discounts, refunds and reversals.
- Taxes and other applicable adjustments.
- Approval process.
- Payout timing and method.
- Dispute resolution and reconciliation.

The system may calculate proposed commission automatically, but it must not invent the rate or silently change the agreement.

13.3 Commission audit

Keep a traceable record of:

- Order and sale identifiers.
- Payment status and reference.
- Gross sale amount.
- Approved deductions and adjustments.
- Commission basis and calculation.
- Commission earned.
- Commission approved.
- Commission paid.
- Outstanding balance.
- Refunds and reversals.
- Manual adjustments and their reasons.
- Reconciliation status and discrepancies.

The owner must be able to inspect and reconcile records. Sensitive records must be access-controlled and backed up.

The commission system is not financially ready until the end-to-end process has been tested with test transactions and reconciliation evidence.

14. TESTING STANDARD

Testing must be continuous, not postponed until the end of the project.

14.1 Automated checks

As applicable, run:

- Code formatting and linting.
- Type checking.
- Unit tests.
- Integration tests.
- Production build.
- Link and route checks.
- Calculator tests.
- Form validation tests.
- Accessibility checks.
- Dependency and security checks.
- Browser-based end-to-end tests.

Tests must fail clearly and report enough information to investigate the failure.

14.2 Manual tests

Test the actual user journey on Android and relevant mobile browsers:

- Home page opens.
- Navigation works.
- Product search and filters work.
- Prices and units display correctly.
- Calculator totals are correct.
- Enquiry forms validate and submit.
- Error messages are understandable.
- Support fallback works.
- Social and contact links open the intended destinations.
- Pages remain usable with a slow or unstable connection.
- The layout works at common phone widths.

14.3 Regression tests

When a problem is corrected, add a test for it when practical so the same problem is less likely to return.

A passing test suite does not establish that every possible user journey is correct. Record the coverage and any untested areas.

